  "body": "I'm reading through https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#timer-initialisation-steps to review an implementation in Servo and having a hard time understanding the role of the timer nesting level in regards to repeating timers. In particular, it looks like any any call to `setTimeout` or `setInterval` will yield a task with a timer nesting value of 1; however, given that a repeating timer automatically calls the timer initialization steps from inside the task, this looks like the timer nesting level for said repeating timer will monotonically increase each time the timer repeats. Is that actually the behaviour that is desired?\n",
